# Project Rule: Figma-Aligned TypeScript Design System

> **Note**: For detailed workflows, step-by-step guides, and code examples, see `AGENTS.md` in the project root.

## Source of Truth
- Figma tokens and components are the primary reference.
- Token files exported from Figma are stored in `Design Tokens Figma/` directory.
- Always check Figma first before creating or modifying components.
- Do not introduce new design values unless they match Figma or are approved extensions.

## Token Usage
- All style values must use CSS variables: `var(--token-name)` (e.g., `var(--bg-primary)`, `var(--spacing-400)`).
- Never use hard-coded values: no hex codes, pixel values, or arbitrary durations.
- Run `npm run build:tokens` after Figma token updates.
- Validate with `npm run validate:css-vars` before committing.

## Design Tokens
- See `design-tokens-rule.md` for comprehensive guidelines on using Figma variables and design tokens

## Component Standards

### File Structure
- Component: `packages/beacon-ui/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx` (PascalCase)
- Documentation: `src/app/components/[component-name]/page.tsx` (kebab-case)
- Preview: `src/components/[ComponentName]Preview.tsx`
- Controls: `src/components/[ComponentName]Controls.tsx`
- Export: Add to `packages/beacon-ui/src/index.ts`

### Code Requirements
- Named exports only: `export function ComponentName()` (never default exports)
- Extend HTML props: `ComponentPropsWithRef<"element">`
- Always call `useThemeSafe()` at component start
- Pure React functions, no side effects in render
- TypeScript interfaces for props (no `any`)
- Inline styles with `React.CSSProperties`, all values use tokens
- Use `useMemo` for computed styles when dependencies change
- Support `className` and `style` props

### Figma Alignment
- Map directly to Figma definition
- Props reflect Figma variants, states, and interactions exactly
- Strict naming consistency with Figma (case-sensitive)

### Accessibility & Theme
- WCAG 2.1 AA compliance required
- Proper ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation, focus management
- Work in both light and dark themes
- Support all hue variants (primary, success, warning, critical)

## Documentation Requirements
- Follow structure from `src/app/components/button/page.tsx`
- Required sections: Overview, Interactive Playground, Anatomy, Variants & States, Usage Guidelines, API Reference, Usage Examples
- Use `PageLayout`, `CodeCopyButton`, `SyntaxHighlighter` components
- All code examples must be valid TypeScript, use tokens, and be copyable

## Reference Existing Components
- See `packages/beacon-ui/src/components/Button.tsx` for component patterns
- See `packages/beacon-ui/src/components/Card.tsx` for styling patterns
- See `src/app/components/button/page.tsx` for documentation structure

## Quality Checks
- Run validation commands (see `AGENTS.md` for details)
- Verify tokens, types, Figma alignment, documentation completeness, accessibility, theme support